    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57315" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῐβώριον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seed-vessel of the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολοκασία</span>, a kind of
				<u>Nvmphaea</u>, containing the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύαμος Αἰγύπτιος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				81.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				105.18
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἢ κιβώτιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					2.106
				</span></i>
			; of the plant itself, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.57
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>cup</i>, either from the material or the shape, <i><span class="en">
				Did.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.477f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hegesand.
				21
			</span></i>; used liturgically, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Par.</u>
				1.1110
			</span></i>.</div>
